{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The 1/4-20 machine screws and M6 bolt assortment felt useful because they could work with my UNC and metric rivet nuts, provided the threads, lengths, and mounting details match.",
    "The CA glue felt like a natural addition to my epoxy and adhesive tapes because quick bonds could help with small fabrication and repair projects."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The filament assumes I own and use a 3D printer, while my history only establishes an interest in hands-on fabrication.",
    "The long lag screws, low-pressure gauge, and specific-gauge electrical connectors require particular projects that my recent purchases do not establish.",
    "Small screw packs and lock washers are relevant, but relevance alone does not give me a reason to buy more when my existing assortments may already cover the job."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My repeated fastener purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to offer more fasteners without enough attention to what they would add to my existing supplies.",
    "My interest in tools and fabrication seems to have been stretched into assumed needs for printing, pressure measurement, and electrical wiring."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters: thread system, diameter, length, and head shape determine whether a fastener will actually work with my rivet nuts and assemblies.",
    "I have repeatedly chosen assortments, so a useful range of sizes or lengths is more compelling than another large pack of one size without a specific need.",
    "Complementing supplies I already use feels more useful than duplicating them; a quick-setting adhesive adds a different capability alongside my epoxy and tapes."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and fabrication interests, but sometimes assumed specific equipment or projects and overlooked whether another supply would add practical value."
}"}
